# fifo_frame_underflow: A barrier count whose barriers do not fit the length faults the command: its stamp is pushed and faulted (the separate "insufficient bytes" check tests the same condition, so it never fires). Only the header is consumed: with length 12 and one barrier, the next command parses cleanly; with length 16 and two barriers, the header's 4 extra bytes become the start of the next header, here a NOP (stamp 5) the guest spelled across the boundary.
{"op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_gpa": "0x40008000", "stamp_slots": 1, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"off": "0x1034", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0xf5"}
